.TH HOTEL 6.SH NAMEhotel \- the hotel-building board game.SH SYNOPSIS\fBhotel\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONA board game of building hotel chains and trading their shares, in themanner of Acquire.  Each player holds numbered tiles and starts with$6000.  On your turn you play a tile onto the grid\fR(\fBWhich tile to play?\fR);\fRtiles side by side found a hotel, of seven chains A to G, and a tilethat joins two chains merges them, paying majority bonuses to thebiggest shareholders of the one swallowed.  Then you buy shares\fR(\fBWhat to buy?\fR),\fRat the price the table shows for each chain.  When the game ends it shows thefinal standings..PPThe board, the chains with their share prices and your holdings and cashare all on one screen.  Control-C gets out; the game asks\fBAre you sure you want to quit? (Y/N)\fRfirst..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR